    "traits": {
      "value": [
        {
          "resource_id": "monster_trait",
          "stats": {
            "trait_name": {
              "value": "Divine Revulsion"
            },
            "trait_description": {
              "value": "(emotion, fear, mental)\n\nIf a redcap sees a creature brandish a religious symbol of a good deity (which requires an interact action by that creature) or use one to cast a divine spell, the redcap must attempt a 19 Will save. It then becomes temporarily immune to all brandished religious symbols for 10 minutes.\n\n- **Critical Success:** The redcap is unaffected.\n- **Success:** The redcap is frightened 2.\n- **Failure:** The redcap gains the fleeing condition for 1 round and is frightened 4."
            },
            "id": "72c85013-6b51-47a3-9315-878503b21def",
            "updated_at": {
              "value": "2026-03-19T22:58:50.064440"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "resource_id": "monster_trait",
          "stats": {
            "trait_name": {
              "value": "Red Cap"
            },
            "trait_description": {
              "value": "(necromancy, primal)\n\nA redcap's woolen hat is dyed with the blood of its victims.\n\nIf the redcap loses its cap, it no longer benefits from fast healing and takes a \u20134 status penalty to its damage rolls. It can create a new cap in 10 minutes, but that cap doesn't grant its powers until the redcap has turned it red with Blood Soak. A cap has no benefit for creatures other than the redcap who made it."
            },
            "id": "d75f1ed3-0fc4-4be7-9bb4-9690cf746bc6",
            "updated_at": {
              "value": "2026-03-19T22:58:50.064440"
            }
          }
        }
